  "notes": "Takes the pattern AはBに{勝|まさ}る (A surpasses B). Often used in written or somewhat formal contexts. The opposite is {劣|おと}る (to be inferior).\n\nKEY PATTERNS:\n・AはBに{勝|まさ}る — A surpasses B\n・～に{勝|まさ}るとも{劣|おと}らない — at least as good as, no less than\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n・{何|なに}にも{勝|まさ}る — surpassing everything, above all else\n・{言葉|ことば}に{勝|まさ}る — beyond words\n・{数|かず}に{勝|まさ}る — superior in numbers\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n・{優|すぐ}れる — to excel, to be outstanding\n・{超|こ}える — to exceed, to surpass (more general, less literary)",
